import java.io.BufferedReader;
import java.io.InputStreamReader;
import java.net.HttpURLConnection;
import java.net.URL;

public class ClassX {
    private static final String SSRF_PATTERN = "^(http|https):\\/\\/(?!localhost|127\\.0\\.0\\.1|0\\.0\\.0\\.0)"; // Regex pattern for SSRF prevention

    /**
     * Hakee sisältöä URL-osoitteesta.
     *
     * Toiminto estää pääsyn paikalliseen silmukointiosoitteeseen estääkseen SSRF:n.
     * @param urlString URL-osoite, josta datan haku toimitetaan
     * @return sisältö URL-osoitteestä, muuten null jos tapahtuu virhe
     */
    public static String fetchData(String urlString) {
        if (urlString == null || !urlString.matches(SSRF_PATTERN)) {
            return null; // Return null if the URL doesn't match the SSRF prevention pattern
        }

        try {
            URL url = new URL(urlString);
            HttpURLConnection connection = (HttpURLConnection) url.openConnection();
            connection.setRequestMethod("GET");
            connection.setRequestProperty("User-Agent", "Mozilla/5.0"); // Custom user-agent

            if (connection.getResponseCode() != HttpURLConnection.HTTP_OK) {
                System.out.println("Failed to retrieve data from URL: " + urlString + ". Status code: " + connection.getResponseCode());
                return null; // Return null if the response code is not OK
            }

            BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(connection.getInputStream()));
            StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();
            String line;
            while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                result.append(line);
            }
            reader.close();
            return result.toString();

        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.out.println("An error occurred while fetching data from URL: " + urlString + ". Error message: " + e.getMessage());
            return null; // Return null in case of any exception
        }
    }
}
```

This Java program defines a method `fetchData` that safely retrieves content from an HTTP URL by checking if the URL matches a regex pattern (`SSRF_PATTERN`) to prevent Secure Sockets Layer/Transport Layer Security (SSL/TLS) Re-Entrancy attacks. If the pattern matches, it proceeds to establish a connection, retrieves information from the URL, and returns it as a string. It also handles exceptions such as network errors or invalid URLs and prints appropriate messages for error handling.

